{
 "description": "The jukebox's track catalogue (core/music/jukebox/catalogue.py): every complete theme a playlist can hold, with its source, its name and the limits and defaults of the playlists. Track ids are stable for ever (never renumbered or reused; a removed track stays with retired). A name is a monster id, a map id or a message (arc, file, id: the game's own texts, read in each language) or text in the five languages, with an optional suffix (a variant) in the five languages. A text name is the mod's own: the game's texts hold no such name, and the suffixes (1), (2) and the numbers are neutral. A message id is the index in the message file as the reader numbers it. needs: a ported monster's key (a build without that port lacks the track). replaced: the villages' and halls' music requests the jukebox takes over (filled by the reverse engineering). provisional: the name is a guess of the place the song plays in, not proven.",
